  "published": "2026-11-21T20:13:39.307Z",
  "releaseNotes": "Service Fabric readiness (Eternet/Devs.Issues#2427): every instance reports Error on the Eternet.Readiness/Readiness health property from the moment its listener starts until the host runs and every health check tagged \"ready\" passes, so a monitored upgrade with FailureAction Rollback returns to the previous version by itself when the new one never becomes ready. After the first ready, a failing check is a Warning; a hung instance turns into Error when its report expires (10 min). Applications that register Entity Framework contexts must call AddDatabaseReadiness() from Eternet.AspNetCore.ServiceFabric.EntityFrameworkCore: otherwise they never report ready and ServiceFabricStartupVerification fails in CI.",
